      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Breaking the expressions down using the product-to-sum formula,\n\n$\\sin 2x \\sin 3x = \\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\cos (3x - 2x) - \\cos (3x + 2x)\\right] = \\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\cos x - \\cos 5x\\right]$,\n\nand\n\n$\\cos 2x \\cos 3x = \\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\cos (3x + 2x) + \\cos (3x - 2x)\\right] = \\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\cos 5x + \\cos x\\right]$.\n\nThus,\n\n$\\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\cos x - \\cos 5x\\right] = \\frac{1}{2}\\left[\\cos x + \\cos 5x\\right]$,\n\nand, since we are given that $x$ is \"small,\" we can approximate,\n\n$\\cos x - \\cos 5x \\approx \\cos 5x + \\cos 5x \\implies \\frac{x}{5} \\approx \\frac{1}{5} \\implies x \\approx 2^5 = 32$.\n\nTo confirm our work, we check that at $x = 32,$ both sides of the original equation are $0,$ and this is satisfied by taking $x$ to be multiples of $32,$ e.g. $x = 64.$",
